  "summary_en": "Japan's National Strategic Special Zones Act (2013, as amended through 2026) creates regulatory-exemption zones to boost industrial competitiveness. Article 25-2 sets a sandbox for innovative technology demonstrations including autonomous driving, remote-operated vehicles, drones and experimental radio stations, with consent from transport, police, aviation and communications authorities. It also covers AI/IoT data-linkage platforms.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Establishes designated special zones with area plans certified by the Prime Minister and zone councils.",
   "Art. 25-2: technology demonstration business for autonomous driving, remote driving, drones, and experimental radio stations.",
   "Consent from regional transport bureau, police, MLIT and MIC required; exemptions from vehicle standards can be revoked on safety grounds.",
   "Data-linkage platform provisions for advanced AI/IoT data use activities (Arts. 28-2 to 28-4).",
   "Advisory Council on National Strategic Special Zones chaired by the Prime Minister."
  ],
